    "question": {
      ":question/id": "140d1b59-a53d-5b25-b30e-473d92d498c5",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n\n$$\n\\left(\\sin\\left(\\frac{11 \\pi}{12}\\right)+\\cos\\left(\\frac{11 \\pi}{12}\\right)\\right)^2\n$$\n\n$$\n\\left(\\sin\\left(\\frac{11 \\pi}{12}\\right)+\\cos\\left(\\frac{11 \\pi}{12}\\right)\\right)^2=\n$$\n{{value}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Expand the square and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\nSet $x=\\frac{11 \\pi}{12}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\sin x+\\cos x)^2 &= \\sin^2 x+2\\sin x\\cos x+\\cos^2 x \\\\ &=1+2\\sin x\\cos x \\\\ &=1+\\sin(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sin x\\cos x &=\\sin(2x) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{11 \\pi}{6}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute this exact value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(\\sin\\left(\\frac{11 \\pi}{12}\\right)+\\cos\\left(\\frac{11 \\pi}{12}\\right)\\right)^2&=1+\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0032ed76-86f7-59d2-a23c-e41fb531080f",
